     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Comments from Slack:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "content": [
           {
            "text": "Peter Winckles  3:16 PM",
            "type": "text"
           },
           {
            "type": "hardBreak"
           },
           {
            "text": "@awoods That is currently supported by providing a custom ObjectIdPathMapper implementation. However, it is my understanding that the intent is that all storage layouts are mapped to an OCFL extension spec. It which case, it's probably best to punt on storage layout related tickets until the spec language is more clear and there are some layout extensions.",
            "type": "text"
           }
          ],
          "type": "paragraph"
         },
         {
          "content": [
           {
            "text": "awoods  3:18 PM",
            "type": "text"
           },
           {
            "type": "hardBreak"
           },
           {
            "text": "@Peter Winckles: So... probably what will happen, is the author of that ticket (NLM) will eventually define their own ObjectIdPathMapper and create/use an associated layout extension.",
            "type": "text"
           }
          ],
          "type": "paragraph"
         },
         {
          "content": [
           {
            "text": "Peter Winckles  3:19 PM",
            "type": "text"
           },
           {
            "type": "hardBreak"
           },
           {
            "text": "They'd have to write a custom implementation now. If a spec existed, I'd be willing to add it to the library.",
            "type": "text"
           }
          ],
          "type": "paragraph"
         },
         {
          "content": [
           {
            "text": "awoods  3:21 PM",
            "type": "text"
           },
           {
            "type": "hardBreak"
           },
           {
            "text": "Sounds good. One thing that we can do now is to get a well-defined specification of behavior/mapping that they are looking for.",
            "type": "text"
           }
          ],
          "type": "paragraph"
         },
         {
          "content": [
           {
            "text": "Peter Winckles  3:21 PM",
            "type": "text"
           },
           {
            "type": "hardBreak"
           },
           {
            "text": "yep",
            "type": "text"
           }
          ],
          "type": "paragraph"
         }
        ],
        "type": "blockquote"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "attrs": {
           "accessLevel": "",
           "id": "557058:e5e5c5e0-6548-43bb-82e6-e50570cc5e41",
           "text": "@Doron Shalvi"
          },
          "type": "mention"
         },
         {
          "text": ", with that said, would you be able to define the exact mapping that you would like to see?",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
